{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_consumercontroller", "label": "ConsumerController", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Empfaengerseite: nimmt Delivery<T>-Envelopes von einem oder mehreren ProducerControllern, dedupliziert nach (producerId, seq), ruft den Handler und ackt automatisch nach dessen Aufloesung.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_consumercontrolleroptionstype", "label": "ConsumerControllerOptionsType<T>", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Die einzige Einstellung ist der Handler \u2014 Per-Producer-Dedup-State wird intern verwaltet, es gibt keine Buffergroesse und keine Consumer-ID zu konfigurieren.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_handler", "label": "handler(body)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Wird genau einmal pro NEUEM (producerId, seq)-Paar gerufen; der Handler sieht nur den Body \u2014 producerId und seq sind Sache des Controllers. Wer sie fachlich braucht, muss sie durch die eigene Pipeline reichen.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_no_explicit_nack", "label": "Werfen ist der einzige Nack-Mechanismus", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Ein Wurf (oder ein rejected Promise) verhindert den Ack, der resendTimeout-Timer des Producers feuert und sendet dieselbe seq erneut. Eine explizite Nack-Nachricht gibt es nicht.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_duplicate_handling", "label": "Automatische Duplikat-Behandlung", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Kommt dasselbe (producerId, seq) erneut an, ueberspringt der Controller den Handler und sendet den Ack erneut \u2014 kein Anwendungscode noetig. Fuer fachliche Idempotenz ueber Restarts hinweg muss die verarbeitete seq neben dem Business-State persistiert werden, denn die In-Memory-Dedup ist beim Restart weg.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_out_of_order_handling", "label": "Out-of-order handling (contiguous + above)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Der Controller haelt eine contiguous-High-Watermark plus eine Menge bereits zugestellter Out-of-order-seqs darueber; jede neue seq wird gegen beide geprueft. Es gibt keine feste Buffergroesse und kein stilles Verwerfen \u2014 der Producer retransmittiert, bis der Handler aufloest und der Ack landet.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_per_producer_dedup", "label": "Per-Producer-Dedup-State", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Jeder Producer fuehrt seine eigene seq; der Consumer haelt ein eigenes (contiguous, above)-Paar pro producerId, sodass die seq-Raeume zweier Producer nicht kollidieren.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_cluster_aware_placement", "label": "Consumer nahe an seinen Daten platzieren", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "rationale": "Die consumer-Ref darf auf einen Remote-Consumer zeigen; der Cluster-Transport serialisiert die Envelopes und der Ack-Pfad nutzt denselben Transport rueckwaerts. Cross-Cluster ist fuer durchsatzgebundene Workloads okay, kostet aber eine Runde pro Ack.", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_consumercontroller", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_consumercontrolleroptionstype", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_consumercontrolleroptionstype", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_handler", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_consumercontroller", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_duplicate_handling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_consumercontroller", "target": "docs_src_content_docs_delivery_consumer_controller_out_of_order_handling", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/src/content/docs/delivery/consumer-controller.mdx", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_src